{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.11", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.11"}, "paraphrase": "Knowledge of the inner self comes from realizing the oneness of guru, mantra, deity, self, mind and breath.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "sound", "body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "original": {"text": "gurumantradevatātmamanaḥpavanānām aikyaniṣphālanād antarātmavittiḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:unity-of-guru-mantra-deity-self"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.12", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.12"}, "paraphrase": "Bliss is the form of Brahman and it resides in the body; the five 'M's manifest it; worship with them is to be done in secret, and making it public leads to hell. (Summary only.)", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancamakara", "cpt:srividya-secrecy"], "practices": ["prc:pancamakara"], "obstacles": ["obs:prakatya"], "disputes": ["dsp:pancamakara-literal-or-substitute"], "restricted": true, "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.13", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.13"}, "paraphrase": "From firmness of contemplation (bhāvanā) comes the power of command (ājñā-siddhi).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "original": {"text": "bhāvanādārḍhyād ājñāsiddhiḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "terms": ["trm:bhavana", "trm:ajna-siddhi"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.14-25", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.14-25"}, "paraphrase": "The conduct of the initiate: no censure of any philosophical school; disregard of no one; the secret told only to a worthy disciple; constant holding of the vidyā; constant immersion in Śiva-hood; avoidance of desire, anger, greed, delusion, pride, envy, unsanctioned violence, theft and what the world detests; worship of one guru without doubt; non-possessiveness everywhere; action done without regard to fruit; omission of non-obligatory rites; continuation of the daily worship even when the five 'M's are unavailable; fearlessness everywhere.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:srividya-conduct"], "obstacles": ["obs:arisadvarga", "obs:sarvadarsana-ninda", "obs:samsaya"], "practices": ["prc:srividya-samaya-conduct"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.2", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.2"}, "paraphrase": "The blessed Paramaśiva, having in play composed the eighteen sciences beginning with the Veda and all the philosophical schools, taking on the corresponding states, was questioned by the Goddess Bhairavī, made of consciousness and not different from himself, and through his five faces set forth the five transmissions (āmnāya), the essence of the highest truth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:amnayas-srividya"], "terms": ["trm:amnaya"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.26-28", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.26-28"}, "paraphrase": "All that is knowable is the oblation, the senses are the ladles, the powers are the flames, one's own self is Śiva, the fire, and oneself is the offerer; the fruit is awareness of consciousness free of objects; there is nothing higher than gaining the self.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ultimate"], "original": {"text": "sarvaṃ vedyaṃ havyam indriyāṇi srucaḥ śaktayo jvālāḥ svātmā śivaḥ pāvakaḥ svayam eva hotā // nirviṣayacidvimṛṣṭiḥ phalam // ātmalābhān na paraṃ vidyate", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "practices": ["prc:antaryaga"], "concepts": ["cpt:body-as-sricakra"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.30", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.30"}, "paraphrase": "The Veda and the other sciences are public, like courtesans; this vidyā is hidden in all the schools.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "original": {"text": "veśyā iva prakaṭā vedādividyāḥ / sarveṣu darśaneṣu gupteyaṃ vidyā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:srividya-secrecy"], "disputes": ["dsp:vedic-status-of-tantra"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.31-33", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.31-33"}, "paraphrase": "The wise should by all means take initiation. Initiations are three: śāktī, by the entry of power; śāmbhavī, by the placing of the (guru's) foot; māntrī, by the imparting of mantra; all should be given — or, some say, any one.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-diksas"], "terms": ["trm:diksa"], "practices": ["prc:srividya-diksa"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.35-36", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.35-36"}, "paraphrase": "In initiation the guru contemplates on the disciple's head the red and white feet, adorning his whole body washed in their nectar, then meditates on a wave of light blazing like fire from the base to the aperture of Brahmā and burns away the disciple's sins and bonds with its rays.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "practices": ["prc:srividya-diksa"], "obstacles": ["obs:eight-pasas"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.39-41", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.39-41"}, "paraphrase": "The guru whispers the Bālā mantra into the disciple's right ear and then the chosen mantra; gives him a name of two to four syllables ending in '-ānandanātha'; and before the Bālā teaching gives him his own pādukā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "sound"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:bala", "trm:paduka", "trm:anandanatha"], "paths": ["pth:srividya-krama-diksa"], "practices": ["prc:srividya-diksa", "prc:guru-paduka-puja"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.4", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.4"}, "paraphrase": "The universe is the thirty-six principles.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "original": {"text": "ṣaṭtriṃśattattvāni viśvam", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:thirty-six-tattvas"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.42-43", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.42-43"}, "paraphrase": "Having taught the rules of conduct and touched the disciple's heart-consciousness, the guru embraces him, smells his head and makes him his own self; the disciple, contemplating fullness, fulfilled, honours the guru with wealth as he can and becomes one who knows what is to be known, entitled to all mantras.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-diksas"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.5", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.5"}, "paraphrase": "Śiva clothed in body and coverings is the individual soul (jīva); Śiva free of coverings is Paraśiva.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "original": {"text": "śarīrakañcukitaḥ śivo jīvo niṣkañcukaḥ paraśivaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:five-kancukas"], "terms": ["trm:kancuka", "trm:jiva"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.6", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.6"}, "paraphrase": "Awareness of oneself (svavimarśa) is the goal of human life.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "original": {"text": "svavimarśaḥ puruṣārthaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "terms": ["trm:svavimarsa"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.7-8", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.7-8"}, "paraphrase": "Words made of letters are eternal; mantras have inconceivable power.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "original": {"text": "varṇātmakā nityāḥ śabdāḥ // mantrāṇām acintyaśaktitā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "terms": ["trm:mantra"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:1.9-10", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "1.9-10"}, "paraphrase": "All success comes through the tradition (sampradāya) and faith (viśvāsa); validity consists above all in faith.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "original": {"text": "saṃpradāyaviśvāsābhyāṃ sarvasiddhiḥ // viśvāsabhūyiṣṭhaṃ prāmāṇyam", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "terms": ["trm:sampradaya", "trm:visvasa"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:10.82", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "10.82"}, "paraphrase": "One steadfast in kula who knows all this and performs it duly has accomplished everything; at the body's fall it makes no difference whether it is in an outcaste's house or in Kāśī — he is liberated while living.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "death-dying"], "original": {"text": "itthaṃ viditvā vidhivad anuṣṭhitavataḥ kulaniṣṭhasya sarvataḥ kṛtakṛtyatā śarīratyāge śvapacagṛhakāśyor nāntaraṃ jīvanmuktaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "GOS 22 (GRETIL e-text)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:10.83", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "10.83"}, "paraphrase": "Whoever studies this ten-section great Upaniṣad, the whole treasure of the great Traipura doctrine, becomes the performer of all sacrifices; whatever rite he studies, by it his sacrifice is accomplished.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "disputes": ["dsp:vedic-status-of-tantra"], "notes": "Arthavāda-style praise of study.", "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:2.2", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "2.2"}, "paraphrase": "Rising in the hour before dawn, the initiate contemplates the guru's feet in the thousand-petalled lotus of the crown, his whole body flooded by the nectar flowing from them; then meditates on Gaṇapati in the heart, and after the morning duties offers libations.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:srividya-nitya-krama", "prc:guru-paduka-puja"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:3.10", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "3.10"}, "paraphrase": "In the great cakra the worshipper contemplates and honours, with forty-four mantras, the Goddess's world: the ocean of nectar, the jewel island, gardens of wish-trees, the jewelled ramparts, halls and pools of nectar, bliss and self-awareness, the great lotus forest, the palace of wish-gems whose four doors are the four transmissions, and the couch whose legs are Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra and Īśvara and whose plank is Sadāśiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:manidvipa-srinagara", "cpt:five-corpse-seat", "cpt:amnayas-srividya"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:parasurama-kalpasutra:4.5", "source": "src:parasurama-kalpasutra", "location": {"ref": "4.5"}, "paraphrase": "The Goddess is served with sixty-four royal services (catuḥṣaṣṭy-upacāra): ornaments removed, anointing with oil, bath, garments, unguents, flowers, jewels from crown to foot, the noose, goad, sugarcane bow and flower arrows, mounting the great cakra with the enclosure deities dressed like her, sitting on Kāmeśvara's lap, drink, betel, lights, parasol, fans, mirror and the rest.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "devotion"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:catuhsasti-upacara"], "terms": ["trm:upacara"], "speaker": "Paraśurāma (by tradition)", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
